WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.785 --> 00:00:13.527
Not only did Meg look different at Annie's party, she acted differently, too.

2
00:00:14.348 --> 00:00:20.112
She walked with her shoulders pulled back proudly, coolly acknowledging people in an aloof manner as she passed

3
00:00:20.152 --> 00:00:26.676
them. When it came to dancing, Meg was selective, choosing only those partners who looked wealthy and handsome.

4
00:00:27.528 --> 00:00:32.830
She loved all the attention she was getting as she tossed her head back and laughed loudly (almost

5
00:00:32.930 --> 00:00:39.011
as loud as Jo) while dancing, quite aware that some of the other girls were jealously staring and

6
00:00:39.071 --> 00:00:39.971
whispering about her.

7
00:00:39.991 --> 00:00:45.513
"Oh, I need to rest my feet," Meg gasped to her dance partner, who happened to be Annie's

8
00:00:45.593 --> 00:00:46.413
older brother Ned.

9
00:00:47.354 --> 00:00:52.375
"Only if you promise to let me have the next dance," Ned said, leading her to some chairs.

10
00:00:53.175 --> 00:00:59.194
Touching his shoulder lightly, as she had seen Sallie do, Meg said in a flirty voice, "I'll think

11
00:00:59.254 --> 00:00:59.695
about it.

12
00:01:00.175 --> 00:01:01.997
Now be a pet and get me a drink."

13
00:01:02.938 --> 00:01:06.541
Ned happily obliged while Meg collapsed onto a chair next to Sallie.

14
00:01:06.561 --> 00:01:11.365
"Meg, you are the darling of the party tonight," Sallie giggled.

15
00:01:12.286 --> 00:01:16.349
Meg lightly touched her eyes with her handkerchief, being careful not to erase her make-up.

16
00:01:16.369 --> 00:01:20.152
"I have never had so much fun," she confessed.

17
00:01:20.172 --> 00:01:24.336
"Well, I think Ned really likes you," Sallie whispered.

18
00:01:25.220 --> 00:01:28.843
Meg looked over at Ned who was carrying two drinks over to where she sat.

19
00:01:29.864 --> 00:01:33.387
Ned was a tall, handsome young man, about two years older than Meg.

20
00:01:34.348 --> 00:01:38.752
She knew from Annie that their parents were hoping he would find a suitable wife and marry in

21
00:01:38.772 --> 00:01:39.753
the very near future.

22
00:01:40.754 --> 00:01:43.796
Meg hoped she might be that special someone he was looking for.

23
00:01:43.816 --> 00:01:46.198
"Here you go," Ned said.

24
00:01:46.579 --> 00:01:48.040
As he handed the glass to Meg.

25
00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:50.862
However, he accidentally spilled some of the drink.

26
00:01:50.882 --> 00:01:52.544
"My dress!"

27
00:01:52.940 --> 00:01:56.382
cried Meg, jumping up and trying to wipe off the mess with her handkerchief.

28
00:01:56.402 --> 00:01:59.043
"I'm such a clumsy baboon!"

29
00:01:59.444 --> 00:02:00.224
exclaimed Ned.

30
00:02:00.924 --> 00:02:06.367
"That's quite all right," reassured Meg, "I'll just step into the ladies' room and clean this off.

31
00:02:07.008 --> 00:02:07.908
Please excuse me."

32
00:02:09.349 --> 00:02:11.670
She left Ned standing there awkwardly with Sallie.

33
00:02:12.771 --> 00:02:15.853
At the Moffats, even the ladies' room was a lavish affair.

34
00:02:16.773 --> 00:02:21.596
Massive gold-trimmed mirrors covered one wall above a solid oak rectangular table.

35
00:02:22.256 --> 00:02:29.540
Gold-plated brushes and hand mirrors, embroidered handkerchiefs, and fresh red roses in crystal vases adorned the table.

36
00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:34.143
Meg sat on one of the dozen plush velvet chairs set out along the table.

37
00:02:35.443 --> 00:02:38.065
On the other side of the wall were the toilets and wash basins.

38
00:02:38.885 --> 00:02:44.168
Glancing at herself in the mirror and admiring her reflection, Meg proceeded to remove the stain on her

39
00:02:44.208 --> 00:02:47.670
dress. Luckily it came off and only needed to be dried.

40
00:02:48.330 --> 00:02:51.412
Meg pressed a handkerchief against the spot to soak up the moisture.

41
00:02:52.380 --> 00:02:55.162
Outside she could hear the faint sounds of a familiar tune.

42
00:02:55.902 --> 00:02:59.584
Humming along, she closed her eyes and imagined she was dancing with Ned.

43
00:02:59.604 --> 00:03:02.606
"Did you see how she flirted with Ned?"

44
00:03:03.146 --> 00:03:05.947
came a high-pitched voice loudly from the washroom area.

45
00:03:06.908 --> 00:03:08.649
The wall blocked Meg's view of the speaker.

46
00:03:09.329 --> 00:03:12.951
For some reason, however, Meg knew the speaker was referring to her.

47
00:03:13.732 --> 00:03:19.395
Then another girl spoke in a lower voice but still clear enough to hear, "That's Belle's dress she's

48
00:03:19.455 --> 00:03:21.736
wearing." "Of course it is.

49
00:03:22.112 --> 00:03:24.394
Her family can't afford anything like that.

50
00:03:24.934 --> 00:03:28.076
I heard she came tonight wearing a cotton summer dress."

51
00:03:29.017 --> 00:03:30.698
Cruel laughter followed that remark.

52
00:03:30.718 --> 00:03:34.120
"Does she think Ned Moffat will ask her out?"

53
00:03:34.541 --> 00:03:36.102
the high-pitched voice asked.

54
00:03:36.122 --> 00:03:37.583
"Heavens, no!

55
00:03:38.003 --> 00:03:41.806
Annie and she are friends, but they would never allow her to become family."

56
00:03:42.726 --> 00:03:48.650
Listening intently to their conversation, Meg did not realize that she had rolled her handkerchief into a tight

57
00:03:48.710 --> 00:03:50.812
ball and was clenching her jaw.

58
00:03:52.272 --> 00:03:54.494
Never had she been so humiliated.

59
00:03:55.375 --> 00:03:59.659
She lowered her shaking hands and slowly turned to look at the stranger staring back at her from

60
00:03:59.679 --> 00:04:00.079
the mirror.

61
00:04:00.900 --> 00:04:04.843
Until that moment, Meg did not realize how different she really looked.

62
00:04:05.564 --> 00:04:07.205
In fact, she was unrecognizable.

63
00:04:07.225 --> 00:04:13.310
"I hate you," she spat to her own pathetic face, which did not look so lovely any more.

64
00:04:14.071 --> 00:04:19.456
Fantasies of marrying Ned Moffat and being the mistress of their impressive estate vanished into thin air.

65
00:04:20.236 --> 00:04:24.779
Delusions of being wealthy and sophisticated like Annie and Sallie faded even more quickly.

66
00:04:25.580 --> 00:04:29.303
Suddenly Meg longed for the comfort and simplicity of her family and home.

67
00:04:29.983 --> 00:04:35.747
Glittering gold and sparkling crystal no longer appealed to her, nor did the lovely silk and lace dresses

68
00:04:35.867 --> 00:04:36.728
of spring colors.

69
00:04:38.129 --> 00:04:42.392
Meg just wanted to be herself and be with those who loved her for who she was.

70
00:04:43.152 --> 00:04:47.436
Blindly trying to find her way out of the Moffats' home, Meg was not looking where she was

71
00:04:47.496 --> 00:04:49.376
going. "Oh!"

72
00:04:49.396 --> 00:04:51.978
she exclaimed as she bumped into someone and fell to the floor.

73
00:04:52.818 --> 00:04:58.401
In her quest to locate the front entrance without attracting attention, Meg had run into someone heading toward

74
00:04:58.441 --> 00:05:00.562
the very festivities she was trying to escape.

75
00:05:02.023 --> 00:05:07.206
"I beg your pardon, Miss," the young man apologized profusely, extending a hand to help her up.

76
00:05:07.226 --> 00:05:12.289
"No, I should be the one apologizing, I wasn't looking Laurie!"

77
00:05:12.749 --> 00:05:15.590
Meg shouted in relief when she saw who her victim was.

78
00:05:16.391 --> 00:05:21.045
Laurie stared at her for a long time, obviously not immediately recognizing her.

79
00:05:21.885 --> 00:05:26.726
When he finally did, his jaw dropped, and he looked at her critically with a disapproving eye.

80
00:05:26.746 --> 00:05:29.667
"Meg? Sweet, innocent Meg?

81
00:05:30.087 --> 00:05:31.127
That can't be you!"

82
00:05:31.468 --> 00:05:32.428
were his first words.

83
00:05:33.168 --> 00:05:35.329
"Laurie, I'm so happy to see you!"

84
00:05:35.629 --> 00:05:36.169
cried Meg.

85
00:05:36.189 --> 00:05:37.989
"I've been so miserable."

86
00:05:38.830 --> 00:05:42.150
Laurie, who was still in shock, demanded, "What happened to you?

87
00:05:42.751 --> 00:05:43.831
What's that on your face?

88
00:05:44.311 --> 00:05:45.751
You look like a stranger to me!"

89
00:05:46.452 --> 00:05:49.328
He was very upset and did not hide the fact.

90
00:05:50.029 --> 00:05:54.350
"Laurie," Meg pleaded, "please, I know I don't look like myself.

91
00:05:54.790 --> 00:05:56.430
I don't feel like myself either.

92
00:05:57.431 --> 00:06:00.892
But right now, I'm so miserable and I have to get out of here.

93
00:06:01.432 --> 00:06:02.652
Won't you please help me?"

94
00:06:03.652 --> 00:06:09.274
Softening as he heard the desperation in Meg's voice, Laurie wrapped his arms around her and comforted her,

95
00:06:09.394 --> 00:06:13.915
saying, "I'm sorry for being so rude, Meg, but I was quite shocked.

96
00:06:14.635 --> 00:06:15.575
Of course, I'll help you.

97
00:06:15.956 --> 00:06:17.436
Come, now, let's get you home."

98
00:06:18.376 --> 00:06:23.299
Like a true gentleman, Laurie, without another remark about her appearance, escorted Meg home.

99
00:06:24.119 --> 00:06:27.321
When Meg got home, she told her family what had happened.

100
00:06:28.622 --> 00:06:32.664
She spoke honestly about how she envied the wealth of her friends and their lifestyle.

101
00:06:33.625 --> 00:06:38.208
Then she told them about overhearing the conversation in the ladies' room that eventually opened her eyes to

102
00:06:38.248 --> 00:06:44.051
reality. "I realize that what I have now may be simple to some, but it's very dear to

103
00:06:44.111 --> 00:06:45.272
me," sniffed Meg.

104
00:06:46.140 --> 00:06:49.942
"I wouldn't change my life now with any amount of money or pretty things."

105
00:06:49.962 --> 00:06:52.963
"And we wouldn't want you any other way.

106
00:06:53.444 --> 00:06:56.545
You're our Meg and we love you," comforted Mother.

107
00:06:57.686 --> 00:07:02.248
Hugging her mother and sisters, Meg gratefully accepted the precious life she had.
